# Workflow Diagram

This folder contains the high-level workflow diagram for the QTC Workflow Queue (WFQ) Administrator Application.

> **Course:** CS3338 — Software Engineering  
> **Project:** QTC Workflow Queue (WFQ) Administrator Application  
> **File:** WorkflowDiagram.png  
> **Diagram Type:** Level 0 Data Flow Diagram (DFD)

---

## Purpose

The purpose of this workflow diagram is to explain, at a high level, how the WFQ Administrator Application works. It shows how the user connects to the UI, how requests are handled by the application, where the data goes, and what system components have access to the workflow data.

---

## Diagram Overview

The workflow diagram includes the following major parts:

| Component | Description |
|---|---|
| QTC Administrator | The authorized user who accesses the WFQ Administrator Application |
| HTTP Requests / Responses | The communication between the user and the web application |
| WFQ Administrator Application | The ASP.NET Core MVC application used to manage workflows |
| T-SQL / EF Core Queries | The database queries sent by the application |
| Workflow Database | The existing SQL Server database that stores workflow information |

---

## Data Flow

1. The QTC Administrator accesses the WFQ Administrator Application through the web interface.
2. The user sends HTTP requests by viewing, creating, editing, or deleting workflow data.
3. The WFQ Administrator Application processes the request.
4. The application sends T-SQL / Entity Framework Core queries to the Workflow Database.
5. The Workflow Database returns SQL results back to the application.
6. The application sends an HTTP response back to the QTC Administrator.

---

